-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CeCWzhkMdmwZdb5tWbNze\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01KxA3oANHzGcAyGfdCz3R9f\",\"name\":\"Read\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/michalis/tornadovm-devoxx2026-cuda-demos/PLAN.md\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":10431,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":16652,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":10431},\"output_tokens\":2,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"9d449b3b-b90b-4cce-bb80-683b5ab25b27\",\"uuid\":\"46bcb687-9ae0-4b18-bd09-5867fb99f006\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-19T17:40:54.033Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CeCWzgv1JxkrwnWJagNNd\"}\n9\t{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01KxA3oANHzGcAyGfdCz3R9f\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"1\\t# Study Plan\\n2\\t\\n3\\t## 1. Objective\\n4\\t\\n5\\tProduce a reproducible body of research, working demos, and draft content for the two Devoxx 2026 talks in `README.md`. The repository is a **TornadoVM CUDA study**, not a framework comparison.\\n6\\t\\n7\\tEvery technical claim must be tied to one of:\\n8\\t\\n9\\t1. current upstream source at a recorded SHA;\\n10\\t2. a runnable probe with captured output;\\n11\\t3. a measured demo result with its environment manifest; or\\n12\\t4. an explicitly labelled hypothesis/open question.\\n13\\t\\n14\\t## 2. System under test\\n15\\t\\n16\\t- TornadoVM: public `develop`, latest at the start of each batch; record `TORNADO_SHA`.\\n17\\t- Backend: `cuda` only.\\n18\\t- NVIDIA GPU: one physical device, recorded with driver/toolkit details.\\n19\\t- CUDA libraries: use the versions actually present and record them.\\n20\\t- Java: record the JDK and TornadoVM runtime configuration.\\n21\\t- GPULlama3.java: use the current reproducible upstream state for LLM work and record its SHA.\\n22\\t\\n23\\tNever use the legacy `ptx` backend. Never silently substitute OpenCL/Metal/CPU execution.\\n24\\t\\n25\\t## 3. Study tracks\\n26\\t\\n27\\t### Track A — Hybrid API fundamentals\\n28\\t\\n29\\tBuild small, deterministic demos in increasing complexity:\\n30\\t\\n31\\tA0. Java GPU kernel / baseline TornadoVM task.\\n32\\tA1. CUDA runtime API access from Java.\\n33\\tA2. Vendor-library call from Java: cuBLAS.\\n34\\tA3. Vendor-library call from Java: cuFFT.\\n35\\tA4. Java kernel + cuBLAS in one execution graph.\\n36\\tA5. Java kernel + cuFFT in one execution graph.\\n37\\tA6. Reusable device buffers / data sharing across tasks.\\n38\\tA7. Error handling, unsupported API behavior, and portability boundaries.\\n39\\t\\n40\\tThe final live demo should be short enough to rebuild or recover during a conference session.\\n41\\t\\n42\\t### Track B — Java LLM inference\\n43\\t\\n44\\tB0. Reproduce current GPULlama3.java build/run instructions.\\n45\\tB1. Establish model/tokenizer/runtime prerequisites.\\n46\\tB2. Reproduce a minimal inference path on TornadoVM CUDA.\\n47\\tB3. Probe FP16, Q8, and Q4 paths; only present paths that work on the current code.\\n48\\tB4. Capture kernel/codegen/profiling evidence useful for explaining the optimization story.\\n49\\tB5. Probe Quarkus integration.\\n50\\tB6. Probe LangChain4j integration.\\n51\\tB7. Produce a presenter-safe end-to-end inference demo with a deterministic prompt and fallback path.\\n52\\t\\n53\\t## 4. Hybrid API verification\\n54\\t\\n55\\tBefore writing content, inspect the actual current TornadoVM tree for:\\n56\\t\\n57\\t- Hybrid API classes and task-graph composition model;\\n58\\t- CUDA runtime bindings;\\n59\\t- cuBLAS/cuBLASLt providers;\\n60\\t- cuFFT provider;\\n61\\t- cuDNN provider;\\n62\\t- cuSPARSE provider;\\n63\\t- CUTLASS provider;\\n64\\t- buffer sharing and stream semantics;\\n65\\t- build/runtime prerequisites;\\n66\\t- current examples/tests.\\n67\\t\\n68\\tDo not assume documentation reflects `develop`. Capture source paths and test/probe commands.\\n69\\t\\n70\\t## 5. Measurement contract\\n71\\t\\n72\\tFor every timed demo:\\n73\\t\\n74\\t- record GPU, driver, CUDA toolkit/runtime, JDK, TornadoVM SHA, demo SHA;\\n75\\t- ensure no competing CUDA process is using the GPU;\\n76\\t- warm up before timing;\\n77\\t- separate compilation/setup time from steady-state execution;\\n78\\t- use deterministic inputs where practical;\\n79\\t- validate output before reporting performance;\\n80\\t- retain raw stdout/stderr and machine-readable results;\\n81\\t- never fabricate missing measurements.\\n82\\t\\n83\\tPerformance is supporting evidence for the talks, not the primary goal. A reliable live demo is more valuable than a fragile benchmark.\\n84\\t\\n85\\t## 6. Content contract\\n86\\t\\n87\\tDraft content must distinguish:\\n88\\t\\n89\\t- **Observed:** reproduced locally and captured.\\n90\\t- **Source-backed:** verified directly in the current repository/source.\\n91\\t- **Documented:** stated by upstream documentation but not independently reproduced.\\n92\\t- **Hypothesis:** plausible but not yet verified.\\n93\\t- **Blocked:** attempted and failed, with the exact reason captured.\\n94\\t\\n95\\tNo claim enters the final talk drafts without an evidence classification.\\n96\\t\\n97\\t## 7. Definition of done\\n98\\t\\n99\\tThe study is complete when:\\n100\\t\\n101\\t- all high-value Hybrid API demos have runnable source and a tested runbook;\\n102\\t- GPULlama3.java current-state reproduction is documented;\\n103\\t- supported quantization paths are verified;\\n104\\t- integration claims have evidence or are explicitly marked blocked;\\n105\\t- both talk drafts have a clear opening, narrative, live-coding sequence, technical explanation, and conclusion;\\n106\\t- every demo has a fallback/recovery path;\\n107\\t- `docs/claims.md` has no unsupported high-confidence claim;\\n108\\t- `scripts/verify.sh` can validate committed evidence without requiring a GPU;\\n109\\t- final rehearsal artifacts are recorded in `results/`.\\n110\\t\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"9d449b3b-b90b-4cce-bb80-683b5ab25b27\",\"uuid\":\"a44d6b3d-1dc5-4801-bf3d-4a8e4f524ab6\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-19T17:40:54.044Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/michalis/tornadovm-devoxx2026-cuda-demos/PLAN.md\",\"content\":\"# Study Plan\\n\\n## 1. Objective\\n\\nProduce a reproducible body of research, working demos, and draft content for the two Devoxx 2026 talks in `README.md`. The repository is a **TornadoVM CUDA study**, not a framework comparison.\\n\\nEvery technical claim must be tied to one of:\\n\\n1. current upstream source at a recorded SHA;\\n2. a runnable probe with captured output;\\n3. a measured demo result with its environment manifest; or\\n4. an explicitly labelled hypothesis/open question.\\n\\n## 2. System under test\\n\\n- TornadoVM: public `develop`, latest at the start of each batch; record `TORNADO_SHA`.\\n- Backend: `cuda` only.\\n- NVIDIA GPU: one physical device, recorded with driver/toolkit details.\\n- CUDA libraries: use the versions actually present and record them.\\n- Java: record the JDK and TornadoVM runtime configuration.\\n- GPULlama3.java: use the current reproducible upstream state for LLM work and record its SHA.\\n\\nNever use the legacy `ptx` backend. Never silently substitute OpenCL/Metal/CPU execution.\\n\\n## 3. Study tracks\\n\\n### Track A — Hybrid API fundamentals\\n\\nBuild small, deterministic demos in increasing complexity:\\n\\nA0. Java GPU kernel / baseline TornadoVM task.\\nA1. CUDA runtime API access from Java.\\nA2. Vendor-library call from Java: cuBLAS.\\nA3. Vendor-library call from Java: cuFFT.\\nA4. Java kernel + cuBLAS in one execution graph.\\nA5. Java kernel + cuFFT in one execution graph.\\nA6. Reusable device buffers / data sharing across tasks.\\nA7. Error handling, unsupported API behavior, and portability boundaries.\\n\\nThe final live demo should be short enough to rebuild or recover during a conference session.\\n\\n### Track B — Java LLM inference\\n\\nB0. Reproduce current GPULlama3.java build/run instructions.\\nB1. Establish model/tokenizer/runtime prerequisites.\\nB2. Reproduce a minimal inference path on TornadoVM CUDA.\\nB3. Probe FP16, Q8, and Q4 paths; only present paths that work on the current code.\\nB4. Capture kernel/codegen/profiling evidence useful for explaining the optimization story.\\nB5. Probe Quarkus integration.\\nB6. Probe LangChain4j integration.\\nB7. Produce a presenter-safe end-to-end inference demo with a deterministic prompt and fallback path.\\n\\n## 4. Hybrid API verification\\n\\nBefore writing content, inspect the actual current TornadoVM tree for:\\n\\n- Hybrid API classes and task-graph composition model;\\n- CUDA runtime bindings;\\n- cuBLAS/cuBLASLt providers;\\n- cuFFT provider;\\n- cuDNN provider;\\n- cuSPARSE provider;\\n- CUTLASS provider;\\n- buffer sharing and stream semantics;\\n- build/runtime prerequisites;\\n- current examples/tests.\\n\\nDo not assume documentation reflects `develop`. Capture source paths and test/probe commands.\\n\\n## 5. Measurement contract\\n\\nFor every timed demo:\\n\\n- record GPU, driver, CUDA toolkit/runtime, JDK, TornadoVM SHA, demo SHA;\\n- ensure no competing CUDA process is using the GPU;\\n- warm up before timing;\\n- separate compilation/setup time from steady-state execution;\\n- use deterministic inputs where practical;\\n- validate output before reporting performance;\\n- retain raw stdout/stderr and machine-readable results;\\n- never fabricate missing measurements.\\n\\nPerformance is supporting evidence for the talks, not the primary goal. A reliable live demo is more valuable than a fragile benchmark.\\n\\n## 6. Content contract\\n\\nDraft content must distinguish:\\n\\n- **Observed:** reproduced locally and captured.\\n- **Source-backed:** verified directly in the current repository/source.\\n- **Documented:** stated by upstream documentation but not independently reproduced.\\n- **Hypothesis:** plausible but not yet verified.\\n- **Blocked:** attempted and failed, with the exact reason captured.\\n\\nNo claim enters the final talk drafts without an evidence classification.\\n\\n## 7. Definition of done\\n\\nThe study is complete when:\\n\\n- all high-value Hybrid API demos have runnable source and a tested runbook;\\n- GPULlama3.java current-state reproduction is documented;\\n- supported quantization paths are verified;\\n- integration claims have evidence or are explicitly marked blocked;\\n- both talk drafts have a clear opening, narrative, live-coding sequence, technical explanation, and conclusion;\\n- every demo has a fallback/recovery path;\\n- `docs/claims.md` has no unsupported high-confidence claim;\\n- `scripts/verify.sh` can validate committed evidence without requiring a GPU;\\n- final rehearsal artifacts are recorded in `results/`.\\n\",\"numLines\":110,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":110}}}\n10\t{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":50,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":50,\"uuid\":\"0b1818c3-9dd3-4bee-afb9-e4a1b397952b\",\"session_id\":\"9d449b3b-b90b-4cce-bb80-683b5ab25b27\"}\n11\t{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":95,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":45,\"uuid\":\"c85dc0b0-b057-4a44-bc16-146243dbb24b\",\"session_id\":\"9d449b3b-b90b-4cce-bb80-683b5ab25b27\"}\n12\t{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CeCX11r32iM9E8MA48Sru\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"\",\"signature\":\"\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":3165,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":27083,\"cache